    "body": "Hmm, I think this could indeed be tested with \"DOMNodeRemovedFromDocument\", which seems to fire on every node of a removed subtree. But that doesn't work in Chromium any longer, so I don't think we should write such a test.\r\n\r\nIn Chromium I think this is implemented as the calls to `ListedElement::ResetFormOwner()` and `HTMLImageElement::ResetFormOwner()` and following the call stack I can't find any tree walking or other recursion inside of the tree walk we do when removing a node. So I think in terms of implementation the spec is closer after this change.\r\n\r\nLet's give it another days to see if anyone has feedback though!",
